I think you miss the point. With speed boots, you DON'T GET HIT. You hit
the monster, you move away, you hit the monster, you move away.....

>>>Second: Wish for good armor. Gray dragon scale mail +2 works well, if you have
>>>it or are AC -5 or better and have something like shield of reflection,
>>>cloak of magic resistance or a wand of polymorph, wish for gauntlets of
>>>dexterity +2. Your Chance to hit depends on dexterity, not on strength.
>>>(Strength accounts for damage).
>
>>DON'T forget the speed boots!  That's "blessed +3 pair of speed boots".
>
>I would never wish for speed boots, most classes have the intrinsic 'fast'
>Archeologist, Elves and Samurais are fast from the beginning, Barbarians,
>Caveman, Knights and Valkyries get fast at the 7th level. Easy to get
>to this level for these classes for an experienced player.
>The other classes get fast when eating a Quantum mechanic.
>Eat them only once, if you're fast and eat one, your speed gets back to
>normal.
>
Intrinsic speed is 1.3X normal. Speed boots give you 2X. Big difference.

>
>>Get speed boots and a ring of levitation.  The ring can be put on to allow
>>water walking (and #dipping), while still giving you the double-speed.
>
>What I've said before about levitation, you can't pick things up when
>levitating. Water walking is better because it allows you to be
>uncautious about pools.
>Besides, speed boots aren't rust proof, can be anoying.

Water walking boots are pretty useless for trap doors and several other
types of traps which are easily avoided by levitation, and which abound
in the castle level and hell. What do you mean, you can't pick things up
while levitating. Of course not. Just take off the ring.

With regard the weapon first, armor second, I used to play that way,
but always found that despite having a great weapon I would still get
killed, usually by a pack of monsters; soldier ants, Uruk-hai, or
while frozen. Getting good armor first gives you a much better chance
early on in the game when you don't NEED a brilliant weapon. And once
you've survived a fair way down, you invariably find an altar, and then
getting a good weapon is a piece of cake.

